  "text": "If you want to create something valuable financially, you don't pursue that. It's best to actually pursue providing useful products and services. If you do that, then money will come as a natural consequence of that, as opposed to pursuing money directly. It's kind of like the pursuit of happiness. You can't sort of pursue happiness directly. You pursue things that lead to happiness, but there's not like direct happiness pursuit. You do things like fulfilling work or study or friends, loved ones. As a result, make you happy. But just be focused on having the output be worth more than the input. That's what really matters, making more than you take.",
